1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,510
This is Codex Micro Glass Guide.

2
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:05,910
I have a very cute, and not inexpensive,

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,690
device on my desk: the Work Louder and

4
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:10,460
OpenAI Codex Micro.

5
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,940
It was the first limited release of a

6
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,470
functional Codex product.

7
00:00:14,930 --> 00:00:16,850
The demonstration videos make it look

8
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:17,930
almost magical.

9
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,110
People fly through their work with a

10
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,460
dial, joystick, glowing Agent keys, and

11
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:26,210
six programmable layers.

12
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,050
I thought, yes.

13
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:31,070
I am going to use this for everything.

14
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:33,700
Then I sat down in front of mine and

15
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:35,120
forgot what the buttons did.

16
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:37,570
That is the problem with programmable

17
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:38,210
hardware.

18
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:41,240
Seeing what it can do is not the same as

19
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,640
remembering how to do it.

20
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:45,240
One button can mean something completely

21
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,730
different on another layer.

22
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:48,840
If I have to stop, search the

23
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:51,400
documentation, and rebuild the map in my

24
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,940
head every time, the friction wins.

25
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,720
And I did not buy a lovely, expensive

26
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:00,180
tool so it could become a dust-gathering

27
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:00,870
paperweight.

28
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:02,710
I am a visual learner.

29
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:05,470
I needed the controls to stay visible

30
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:06,270
while I worked.

31
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:09,280
I needed color, position, and

32
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:11,810
plain-language reminders that I could

33
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,480
understand at a glance.

34
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:17,170
So I built Codex Micro Glass Guide.

35
00:01:18,330 --> 00:01:20,840
It is a translucent Mac guide that

36
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,270
floats above my other apps while I learn

37
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:24,090
the device.

38
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:27,440
I can move it, resize it, and click a

39
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:29,720
control for a simple reminder without

40
00:01:29,790 --> 00:01:30,680
leaving my work.

41
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:33,770
The actual layout is right there: the

42
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,390
white dial, joystick, touch sensor,

43
00:01:36,810 --> 00:01:39,760
layer lights, command buttons, and six

44
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,510
glowing Agent keys.

45
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:44,810
A quick touch cycles through the six

46
00:01:44,890 --> 00:01:45,380
layers.

47
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,010
The three small lights show which layer

48
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:48,890
is active.

49
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:51,200
My labels can match the shortcuts I

50
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:52,180
really use.

51
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,870
I think of it as training wheels made of

52
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:55,450
glass.

53
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,830
The guide stays beside me while

54
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:59,880
repetition becomes familiarity.

55
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:02,390
The point is not to keep reading the

56
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:03,220
guide forever.

57
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,440
The point is to use the hardware until

58
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:08,080
my hands know what to do.

59
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:11,100
The public project includes the Codex

60
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,840
skill and a privacy-safe Mac app

61
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:14,490
template.

62
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:17,630
Personal task names and links stay in

63
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:18,600
your local copy.

64
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,300
And this is not one perfect layout for

65
00:02:21,370 --> 00:02:21,950
everyone.

66
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,570
Rename your layers.

67
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,810
Change the colors.

68
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:26,140
Rewrite the notes.

69
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:29,410
Adapt it for your hands, your brain,

70
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,470
your workflow, and your desk.

71
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:35,120
Then share the privacy-safe ideas that

72
00:02:35,170 --> 00:02:36,510
could help someone else.

73
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:39,600
I built Codex Micro Glass Guide to turn

74
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,830
an exciting piece of hardware into a

75
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,640
tool I will actually use.

76
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:45,760
The skill and source are in the

77
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:46,720
repository.

78
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:49,740
Make it yours, build the muscle memory,

79
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:52,610
and do not let your Codex Micro gather

80
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,120
dust.

81
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:55,480
Independent community project.

82
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:58,090
Not affiliated with or endorsed by

83
00:02:58,210 --> 00:03:00,040
OpenAI or Work Louder.
